      'Turn-flow example: Play is clockwise. The player to the left of the dealer leads any card face-up to start the play pile. On your turn you may either beat the top card (play a higher card of the same suit or one of your own trumps on a different suit) and then play a second card of your choice on top, or pick up cards from the pile (3 if the top is not your trump, 5 if it is your trump but not the ace, or the whole pile if it is the ace of your trump). After a pick-up, the next player must beat the new top card or pick up. If the pile is empty, the next player leads any card. Each player has one assigned trump suit; only your own trumps can beat other suits.',
